WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:06.100
There are certain things we see everyday,

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:08.460
and never give a second thought about their history.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:12.100
But with a little digging, the evolution of everyday objects can be shocking!

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:16.100
If you are a first time viewer, click the red "subscribe" button and enjoy!

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:21.400
Today we are reviewing ten regular objects that look nothing like they used to!

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:22.620
Sunglasses.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:28.060
Before people were using their sunglasses to look cool indoors, they actually served a purpose!

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:33.580
These are the oldest pair of sunglasses ever found and believed to bee 800 years old!

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:39.400
They were designed by Inuits to help protect their eyes from the light that reflected off the ice and snow.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:43.740
The light from this snow could get so DANGEROUS that it could actually blind people!

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:48.980
Thankfully, we have a more attractive way to keep the sun out, and look cool at the same time!

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:50.040
Keys.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:54.520
Metal keys have certainly evolved over the years, but are quickly becoming obsolete,

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:55.940
thanks to technology.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:01:00.020
The first versions of metal keys were simpler than what we see today, and

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:04.760
since having something worth locking up was uncommon in ancient times, having a

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:07.640
key became more of a status symbol than anything else.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:10.800
These days people have so many keys, they can't keep up with them.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:15.480
Not to mention the hundreds of hotel keycards they probably have lying around.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:16.180
Toilet paper.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:22.180
Could you imagine wiping your bottom with a rock? Well, that's exactly what scientists think that these ceramic

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:23.500
disks were used for.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:29.540
It is believed that ancient Romans used hard sponges dipped in vinegar on a stick to clean up after using the

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:30.140
restroom.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:36.160
But, because many of these ceramic disks have been unearthed in several Greek and Roman latrines, it's an

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:40.320
easy conclusion that they were also used as ancient toilet paper.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:43.340
Thankfully, there have been many advances in this department!

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:44.800
High Heels.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:49.140
High heels fist poped up in histoy around 3500 B.C.,

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:55.160
and the have several transformations since.These pair of heels from ancient Rome and Greece were known as

00:01:55.160 --> 00:02:01.100
"Buskins", and were worn by stage performers to help differentiate the social class of individual characters.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:07.280
In the Middle Ages, high heels made of wood known as "pattens", were slipped on so nobles wear their expensive

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:09.800
shoes clean of mud and street litter.

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:15.460
These days, high heels are worn by men and women who wish to spice up an outfit with the sultry footwear.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:16.600
Maps.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:20.360
Considering hundreds of years ago many believed the world was flat.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:25.960
It shouldn't be surprising that maps look completely different, this first entry map shows an Earth that has

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:27.440
much more land than water.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:29.780
The America's aren't even on it.

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:36.200
It wasn't until the late 1600s that we see a map that is closer to the one  we use today and modern times we

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:37.440
don't even use paper maps.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:41.160
Most of the time we rely on our cell phones to tell us where to go.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:42.020
Cars

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:46.640
One of the first cars to hit the road was this 1.1 horse power carriage

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:49.280
that was invented in 1886.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:54.240
Just look at the difference in style and the difference in horse power to what we see today.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:59.820
This car featured 3 tires and a rear engine, and apparently they believed a stick was

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:05.940
the best way to steer. The car has evolved so much that now, 130 years later, we have

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:10.600
over 500 times more horsepower, and luckily for us, a steering wheel.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:12.020
Apple computers.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:18.380
In 1976, one of the world's now most famous and lucrative tech companies was born.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:21.820
Apple, and their first product was the Apple 1 computer.

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:25.160
It looks like something a kid could throw together at their local high school,

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:29.440
but it was considered a huge technological advancement back in the '70's.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:35.320
Thanks to Steve Wozniak's and Steve Job's innovation, we now have Iphones and Macbooks

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:37.720
that put the early Apple computer to shame.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:38.960
Socks.

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:42.920
These days, most people wouldn't be caught dead wearing socks with sandals,

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:45.380
but that wasn't the case 1600 years ago.

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:50.700
In fact, these ancient woolen socks were made by the Egyptians to specifically wear with

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:55.220
sandals. Considering there probably weren't many footwear choices in 400 A.D.,

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:58.340
we can forgive the ancient Egyptians for this fashion faux pas.

00:03:58.660 --> 00:03:59.160
Bra.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:03.320
There is nothing about the words "breast pouches" that sounds appealing.,

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:06.240
but this is what bras were made of hundreds of years ago.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:10.740
This bra from Austria is thought to be around 500 years old.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:17.060
Notice the pouch like shape, and the lack of underwire. And, there doesn't seem to be any adjusting straps,

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:23.300
which means this bra was custom made for its owner. Bras in modern times are still considered torture devices

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:27.300
much like this one probably was, but at least they are much more attractive.

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:28.260
Condoms.

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:33.400
We often hear of the crazy ways people used to prevent birth before condoms were invented,

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:38.880
but we don't often hear about what these original condoms were made from, or what they looked like.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:40.200
That is, until now.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:46.400
This reusable condom is around 370 years old, and is made from sheep skin.

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:51.280
That looks terrifying, and not pleasurable at all. The instructions have been preserved, and

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:55.360
call for it to be cleaned with warm milk to prevent venereal disease.

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:57.000
Ooh, yikes.

00:04:57.080 --> 00:05:00.780
Are you happy that these regular objects looked nothing like they used to?

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:06.520
React in the comment section below, and don't forget to like this video, and subscribe to "The Things".

